## Hints

- E1: `r.rolling(W).cov(m) / m.rolling(W).var()`; expanding twins via
  `.expanding(60)`. Verify truth-recovery: expanding tail ≈ 1.10 ±
  a shrinking band.
- E2: band width = 4·σ_e/(σ_x√W): W = 252 → ≈ 4/√252 ≈ 0.25 wide;
  the observed 5–95% range should be ~70–90% of that (overlapping
  windows correlate the extremes; independent-window algebra would
  overstate it).
- E3: split-sample SEs from ols_fit per segment; the z uses INDEPENDENT
  subsamples (the segment sums are disjoint — that's the point of
  splits over rollings for inference).
- E4: rolling alpha = rolling mean(y − β̂x)... careful: better rolling
  intercept via α̂_t = ȳ_W − β̂_t·x̄_W — all rolling means; annualize
  ×252. Band fraction excluding 0 is usually ~5–10% for megacaps.
